From: BoltWrt maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] build: pin gRPC 1.83.2 security fixes

Keep the v2ray core and plugin at 5.49.0. Update the Go module graph for
gRPC transport fixes (rapid reset and receive-buffer fragmentation), with
checksums generated by go get google.golang.org/grpc@v1.83.2 and go mod tidy.

References:
 https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/security/advisories/GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
 https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/security/advisories/GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc
 https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/security/advisories/GHSA-2v4p-qf9q-27wj

--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 	github.com/golang/protobuf v1.5.4
 	github.com/shirou/gopsutil/v4 v4.26.3
 	github.com/v2fly/v2ray-core/v5 v5.49.0
-	golang.org/x/sys v0.43.0
+	golang.org/x/sys v0.47.0
 	google.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.11
 )
 
@@ -23,12 +23,12 @@
 	github.com/tklauser/go-sysconf v0.3.16 // indirect
 	github.com/tklauser/numcpus v0.11.0 // indirect
 	github.com/yusufpapurcu/wmi v1.2.4 // indirect
-	golang.org/x/crypto v0.50.0 // indirect
-	golang.org/x/mod v0.34.0 // indirect
